From 98c83489bc8bc37292bc850dcc5eb5a12d890fa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:26:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(post): probing hooks for the Haas, Mazak and Siemens
 posts

Voice onProbeMove / onProbeRetreat / onProbeResult in haas.cps (G31,
#5061-#5063, #3000/#3006, G10 L2), mazak.cps (G31 + macro, IF..GOTO with
unique labels, M00 operator stop) and sinumerik.cps (MEAS=1, $AC_MEA,
$AA_MW, SETAL, $P_UIFR settable frames; G58/G59 refused by name), each
from its dialect's public programming documentation. The three posts
no longer start a spindle at 0 rpm (a touch probe states none).
heidenhain.cps keeps the engine's named refusal: its ISO manual states
no skip move or trip-position variable, and no Q parameter is guessed.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/probe_dialects.rs with bore-centre goldens
under golden/nc/{haas,mazak,sinumerik}/ and the Heidenhain refusal.

Fixes #173

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
