From cf6c958d05aa2005e393ef4f2a7dc59e68cf385b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:34:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(post): Haas, Mazak and Sinumerik guard probe
 positioning moves

#174 made the engine refuse every probe op on a post without
onProbeGuard. Haas and Mazak now write each GUARD record as a G31 skip
with a #5061+ position test per moving axis, alarming #3000=3 (Mazak in
its IF[..]GOTOn form); Sinumerik writes a MEAS=1 G1 block and alarms
SETAL(65002) when $AC_MEA[1] shows the probe responded. Each is
distinct from the no-contact alarm. Haas/Mazak fold the target's sign
into the operator (minusU). The three probe_bore_centre goldens gain
only the guard lines (plus Mazak label / Sinumerik block renumbering).

Refs #173

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
